' purpose: bounded offline ordinary per-object fixture custody, without Native authority
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/custody.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/custody.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/input-descriptor.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/input-descriptor.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/custody-chunks.test.mjs
' context: _spec/_plans/ml-runtime-redesign.md sections 12 (historical) and 13 (stream unit).
' scope: standalone ordinary helper; no F9 private initializer or standard-slot ABI.
' validation: Node syntax/tests and PlantUML check/render passed; source reviews accepted.
' readability: FK uses English syllable estimates with explicit engineering-token counts.
' FK: shared-validation note over SOURCE,DESC = 11.2 (24 words, 45 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: acquisition note over SOURCE,PRODUCER = 10.5 (25 words, 45 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: per-object note over ROOT,FILE = 10.8 (26 words, 47 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: cleanup note over SOURCE,PRODUCER = 11.7 (26 words, 49 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: close-uncertainty note over SOURCE,ERROR = 10.1 (28 words, 48 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: producer-trust note over PRODUCER,HOST = 10.8 (26 words, 47 syllables, 2 sentences).
@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Ordinary per-object custody — legacy Buffer or bounded pull stream

actor "Offline caller" as CALLER <<host>>
participant "tooling/native-ingress/\ncustody.mjs" as SOURCE <<app>>
participant "tooling/native-ingress/\ninput-descriptor.mjs" as DESC <<app>>
participant "chunks[Symbol.iterator]()\ncaller-supplied producer" as PRODUCER <<host>>
participant "node:fs / process\nhost runtime" as HOST <<host>>
database "rootPath\nfresh directory" as ROOT <<db>>
database "fixture.bin\nfresh regular file" as FILE <<db>>
participant "CustodyError" as ERROR <<error>>

alt Legacy Buffer entry
  CALLER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : stageFixture(rootPath, {bytes, expectedSha256})
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : start 3.5s deadline; validate path; capture fields once
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : copy bounded Buffer; verify incoming hash before mkdir
else Pull with cleanup
  CALLER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : stageFixtureChunks(rootPath, descriptor, chunks)
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : start 3.5s deadline; validate path
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN DESC : validateFixtureDescriptor(descriptor), before producer access
  DESC ARROW_MAIN DESC : reject proxies via node:util types, without traps
  DESC ARROW_MAIN DESC : inspect prototype, exact own keys and data descriptors
  DESC ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : frozen independent {name, byteLength, sha256} snapshot
end
note right of SOURCE
Absolute normalized non-root path
Buffer length 1..65536; lowercase SHA-256
Intrinsic typed-array length
Bounded native byte copy
end note
note right of DESC
Object.prototype or null prototype
Exactly name, byteLength, sha256; no accessors
name:'fixture.bin'; byteLength:1..65536
sha256:64 lowercase hexadecimal characters
No symbols, URL, destination or authority keys
end note
note over SOURCE, DESC
Both entry points share object validation
to prevent drift between custody policies.
The descriptor module owns the error class;
custody re-exports the same constructor.
end note

group Shared private stage engine; active try/finally
  opt Chunk entry only, before mkdir
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN PRODUCER : guarded acquisition: capture/call Symbol.iterator once
    PRODUCER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : iterator object; store inside guarded action
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN PRODUCER : capture optional callable return BEFORE callable next, once
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : post-action deadline guard; malformed producer => E_SOURCE
  end
  note over SOURCE, PRODUCER
Acquisition stores the iterator before its
deadline check to preserve cleanup on failure.
Capturing return before next preserves cleanup
when next acquisition fails or throws.
  end note

group Fresh root; no collision repair
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : check platform flags; capture effective UID once
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : mkdirSync(rootPath, 0700, recursive:false)
  HOST ARROW_MAIN ROOT : exclusive directory creation
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : open root: RDONLY | DIRECTORY | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : fstat + lstat, bigint:true
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertRoot(named, opened, uid); retain rootBirth
end
note over SOURCE, ROOT
Root security: dev, ino, mode, uid, gid, nlink
Directory, effective UID, exact mode0700
Root binding excludes size and timestamps
end note

group Exclusive file birth and incremental custody
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : open fixture: WRONLY | CREAT | EXCL | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK
  HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : create fixture.bin with mode0600
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : fstat + lstat, bigint:true
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertFileBirth(named, opened, uid)
  note over SOURCE, FILE
Regular file, effective UID, exact mode0600
nlink1; birth size0; named/FD snapshot equal
  end note
  alt Legacy Buffer entry
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : one writeSync, position0, full copied input length
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require full count; no short-write retry
  else Chunk entry: one acquisition; at most 17 next calls
    loop At most 16 data chunks plus required terminal result
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN PRODUCER : guarded captured next with iterator receiver
      PRODUCER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : non-proxy object; own data boolean done
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : if done:false require own data value; else mark completed
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : store completed INSIDE producer action, then deadline guard
      alt done:true
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : exit pull loop; ignore value
      else done:false
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require chunk count <16; Buffer with native length 1..4096
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : intrinsic backing getter requires ordinary ArrayBuffer, not SAB
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : private copy; require cumulative length <= descriptor.byteLength
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : update incremental incoming SHA-256
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : exact writeSync at current offset; no retry
        HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : write this snapshot before the next pull
        SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : advance offset and chunk count; no arrays/concat/replay
      end
    end
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require completed + exact length + complete incoming hash
  end
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : fstat + lstat file; fstat + lstat root
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertFilePhase; birth security unchanged; rootBinding
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : close writer before reader acquisition
end

note over SOURCE, FILE
Content: dev, ino, mode, uid, gid, nlink,
size, mtimeNs, ctimeNs — all bigint
Security fields and size fit unsigned 64-bit
Full equality within each file phase
Birth-to-written comparison: security only
end note
note over ROOT, FILE
Each object retains its own device identity
because parent and file devices may differ.
Stable host paths remain required; checks cannot
protect ancestors against concurrent change.
end note

group Independent readback after writer closure
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : open fixture: RDONLY | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : fstat + lstat, bigint:true
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertFilePhase; full snapshot equals written
  loop Exact positional chunks, at most 4096 bytes each
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : readSync at current offset; require exact count
    HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : read fixture bytes
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : update independent SHA-256; advance offset
  end
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : one-byte EOF probe at expected length
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require EOF and expected readback SHA-256
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : fstat + lstat file, bigint:true
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertFilePhase; full snapshot still equals written
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : close reader; fstat + lstat root
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : rootBinding; prepare frozen DATA_ONLY result
end

group Unconditional descriptor finalization, then producer cleanup
  opt Any guard, I/O or explicit close fails
    SOURCE ARROW_ERROR ERROR : preserve CustodyError; normalize other failures to E_FS
  end
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : finally: close remaining file/root holders once
  note over SOURCE, HOST
Clear holder before each close attempt
Closures bypass deadline and operation guards
At most three total close attempts
  end note
  opt Any close attempt fails
    SOURCE ARROW_ERROR ERROR : E_CLOSE takes priority; no uncertain-close retry
  end
  opt Iterator acquired, not completed, captured return exists
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : clear return holder before invocation; bypass both guards
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN PRODUCER : captured return with iterator receiver, exactly once
    PRODUCER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require non-proxy object with own data done:true; ignore value
    opt Callback throws or cleanup result is invalid
      SOURCE ARROW_ERROR ERROR : E_CLOSE > E_SOURCE_CLEANUP > original; preserve cause chain
    end
  end
  note over SOURCE, PRODUCER
Captured cleanup bypasses cooperative guards
because failure must not suppress finalization.
The callback can block forever, so call bounds
do not establish a runtime lifecycle bound.
  end note
  note right of PRODUCER
No return method: no callback/resource proof
No cleanup after valid done:true, even when
length, hash or post-call deadline checks fail
  end note
end
note over SOURCE, ERROR
Close uncertainty prevents a success result
because descriptor disposition is no longer known.
The helper retains partial roots for inspection;
only the test removes its fresh owned paths.
end note

end

alt Failure recorded
  SOURCE ARROW_ERROR CALLER : throw failure; no result
else All checks and closes succeeded
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : final cooperative deadline guard
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CALLER : frozen ordinary-per-object-v1 / DATA_ONLY
end
note right of CALLER
nativeAuthority:false; installed:false
Point-time byte verification, not immutability
end note
note over SOURCE, HOST
96 ordinary-operation cap; max two owned FDs
Acquisition + <=17 next calls share this cap
Max64KiB: <=16 writes (legacy:1), 17 reads
Three opens/closes; finalizers bypass cap/clock
end note
note over PRODUCER, HOST
Trusted producers may execute arbitrary code
without a sandbox or hard time limit.
Custody call bounds confer no Native authority
and do not prove whole-runtime safety.
end note
@enduml
